\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {12}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {We withdraw the claim that LIBERO-Object is distinctively admissible.} It was always stated as conditional on $\delta $ and Figure~\ref {fig:dependency} drew the window it needed, $[1.17, 1.49)$\,cm. The first direct measurement of $\delta $ on the grasped object lands above that window, and at $2$\,cm more than half the tasks in the other three suites admit a constant too. What survives is \S  \ref {sec:declared} (arithmetic on shipped files), \S  \ref {sec:e1} (no $\delta $ anywhere in it) and Proposition~\ref {prop:lookup} (a theorem). What does not is the \emph  {verdict}.}}{14}{table.caption.52}\protected@file@percent }
