\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Nine self-inflicted errors and their repairs. Every one was found by someone checking a choice rather than a computation, and every one ran in the direction that flattered us. The third is the one we would most expect others to hit: every check we ran had passed, and the defect was in \emph  {when} we looked. The harvester now reports each cell against its planned $n$ and refuses to report an incomplete one.}}{23}{table.caption.74}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:fooled}{{20}{23}{Nine self-inflicted errors and their repairs. Every one was found by someone checking a choice rather than a computation, and every one ran in the direction that flattered us. The third is the one we would most expect others to hit: every check we ran had passed, and the defect was in \emph {when} we looked. The harvester now reports each cell against its planned $n$ and refuses to report an incomplete one}{table.caption.74}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {21}{\ignorespaces What the two diagnostics require. The first two rows are arithmetic on shipped files and are what we would ask a benchmark to publish; the third needs an embodiment and is where our own result is weakest. The scripts are \texttt  {scripts/admissibility.py} and \texttt  {scripts/declared\_vs\_shipped.py}; both read a per-task table of object positions and are ${\sim }150$ lines. Porting them is a matter of writing the reader for another benchmark's state format, not of reimplementing the measurement.}}{24}{table.caption.79}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:portable}{{21}{24}{What the two diagnostics require. The first two rows are arithmetic on shipped files and are what we would ask a benchmark to publish; the third needs an embodiment and is where our own result is weakest. The scripts are \texttt {scripts/admissibility.py} and \texttt {scripts/declared\_vs\_shipped.py}; both read a per-task table of object positions and are ${\sim }150$ lines. Porting them is a matter of writing the reader for another benchmark's state format, not of reimplementing the measurement}{table.caption.79}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {22}{\ignorespaces Three practices, in increasing order of what they cost a benchmark's authors. LIBERO-Spatial already satisfies the second by necessity --- all ten of its targets are the same bowl --- and LIBERO-Object could satisfy it by choice.}}{24}{table.caption.80}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:recs}{{22}{24}{Three practices, in increasing order of what they cost a benchmark's authors. LIBERO-Spatial already satisfies the second by necessity --- all ten of its targets are the same bowl --- and LIBERO-Object could satisfy it by choice}{table.caption.80}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {23}{\ignorespaces Tasks whose identity-bearing object one constant serves, against the tolerance. \textbf  {The separation is real at $1.4$\,cm and gone by $1.9$\,cm}, and those two numbers are our own two measurements of the same assumption (\S  \ref {sec:refute}): task $0$ fails at basket displacements from $1.41$\,cm, task $3$ tolerates $1.91$\,cm. We report the headline at the smaller one, which is the value that favours us. At the larger one LIBERO-Object is still $10/10$ but so are thirteen tasks elsewhere, and the contrast is no longer a separation. Artifact: \texttt  {results/admissibility.json}.}}{24}{table.caption.81}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:deltasens}{{23}{24}{Tasks whose identity-bearing object one constant serves, against the tolerance. \textbf {The separation is real at $1.4$\,cm and gone by $1.9$\,cm}, and those two numbers are our own two measurements of the same assumption (\S \ref {sec:refute}): task $0$ fails at basket displacements from $1.41$\,cm, task $3$ tolerates $1.91$\,cm. We report the headline at the smaller one, which is the value that favours us. At the larger one LIBERO-Object is still $10/10$ but so are thirteen tasks elsewhere, and the contrast is no longer a separation. Artifact: \texttt {results/admissibility.json}}{table.caption.81}{}}
